{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They have provoked Me to jealousy with not a god</b>, with a thing that has no divinity — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 32:21). If so, it alludes to the demons mentioned [in Scripture]. But the correct interpretation is that it says: they provoked Me to jealousy with not a true god, for there is no divinity aside from YHWH, and there is no savior besides Him, as it is said (II Chronicles 15:3), \"and many days for Israel without the God of truth.\"" "<b>They have angered Me with their vanities</b> — the demons. <b>And I will provoke them to jealousy with a no-people</b> — the Chaldeans, as it is said of them (Isaiah 23:13), \"Behold the land of the Chaldeans — this is the people that was not,\" whose meaning is: the people that was not counted as a nation, and the Holy One, blessed be He, raised them up to subdue His world through them, as He said (Jeremiah 51:20), \"You are My mace, a weapon of war.\" <b>In a base nation I will provoke them</b> — Esau, for he is base (naval), and did not remember the covenant of brothers. And it alludes to the two exiles."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:19.474954009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}